artifacts/
TestResults/
StrykerOutput/
verification/out/

# The repo-root .gitignore excludes coverage*.xml and coverage*.json, which would silently eat committed
# Marker test fixtures - fixture-coverage/*/*/coverage.cobertura.xml matches coverage*.xml exactly.
# Keep this negation narrow and anchored to the one folder that needs it. It used to read !**/Fixtures/**
# plus !**/fixtures/**, which also re-included everything under verification/fixtures/ and so cancelled the
# root bin/ and obj/ rules there - 159 build-output files ended up tracked before anyone noticed.
# A pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding this file, so this is
# judging/Skill.Suite.Marker.Tests/Fixtures/**, and only that directory's real spelling is needed.
!Skill.Suite.Marker.Tests/Fixtures/**

# Packed packages are build output, never committed: a session's Contracts package carries hidden tests.
# The leading **/ matters - a pattern containing a slash is anchored to the directory holding this file, so
# plain `local-nuget/*.nupkg` would only match judging/local-nuget and miss every nested module.
**/local-nuget/*.nupkg
**/local-nuget/*.snupkg

